<title>CANADA: Bank of Canada 91-day T-bill yields avg 3.193 pct.</title>
<headline>Bank of Canada 91-day T-bill yields avg 3.193 pct.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1996-10-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Canada said the average yield at this week's auction of C$2.8 billion of 91-day Government of Canada treasury bills due January 30, 1997 was 3.193 percent, up from 3.159 percent last week.</p>
<p>The average yield on C$1.3 billion of 175-day T-bills due April 24, 1997 was 3.400 percent, up from 3.265 percent last week, and on C$1.2 billion of 364-day T-bills due October 30 was 3.681 percent, up from 3.611 percent.</p>
<p>The Bank bought C$725 million three-month, C$150 million six-month and C$125 million one-year bills. It holds C$1.2 billion of C$5.5 billion of bills due Nov. 7.  </p>
